        {
          "path": "_m/g/c/t/m/egremont-cumbria-wp/egremont-station-site-geograph.jpg",
          "filename": "Egremont station site geograph-3453749-by-Ben-Brooksbank.jpg",
          "caption": "Egremont: site of former station, 1994.\nView NE at the roundabout on the A595 Barrow- Whitehaven road. The station had been just up to the lefr here: ex-LNW &amp; Furnees Joint, Whitehaven, Cleator &amp; Egremont line; Moor Row (to left) - Sellafield (to right). The station (and line) had a complex history, being first closed to passengers 7/1/35, but reopened for workmen 11/3/40, for the public 6/5/46 - 16/6/47, but again for workmen 23/5/49 - 6/9/65, for schools 3/3/69. It and the line remained for goods until 15/6/72. (!)",
          "alt": "Egremont: site of former station, 1994.\nView NE at the roundabout on the A595 Barrow- Whitehaven road. The station had been just up to the lefr here: ex-LNW &amp; Furnees Joint, Whitehaven, Cleator &amp; Egremont line; Moor Row (to left) - Sellafield (to right). The station (and line) had a complex history, being first closed to passengers 7/1/35, but reopened for workmen 11/3/40, for the public 6/5/46 - 16/6/47, but again for workmen 23/5/49 - 6/9/65, for schools 3/3/69. It and the line remained for goods until 15/6/72. (!)",
          "width": 2290,
          "height": 1431,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Ben Brooksbank",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Egremont_station_site_geograph-3453749-by-Ben-Brooksbank.jpg",
